# {{.Name}}

A Gibson plugin scaffolded by `gibson component init --kind plugin`.

This plugin is **Go-first** (ADR-0065 R4): `handler.go` declares typed request
and response structs and the handler function; the SDK derives each method's
JSON-Schema contract from those Go types at registration. There is no `.proto`
and no generated code. The plugin declares its name, version and methods in
`handler.go` (ADR-0097). No manifest file exists.

See **[AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md)** for the full contract — the declaration in
code, lifecycle states and the secrets broker. What follows is the quickstart.

## Quickstart

```sh
# 1. Run the hermetic handler test (cassette replay — no daemon, no network)
go test ./...

# 2. Build
make build

# 3. Enrol on first start. The binary does the handshake itself: set two
#    environment variables and start it once (sdk#128). `gibson component
#    register` existed only to read component.yaml and was deleted with it.
export GIBSON_URL=https://<your-platform>
export GIBSON_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=<one-time-token-from-the-dashboard>

# 4. Run. The first start enrols; later starts reuse the persisted host key.
make run
```

## Add a method

1. Add a typed request/response struct pair and a handler func to `handler.go`.
2. Register it with its description:
   `plugin.WithHandler("MyMethod", "What the method does.", myHandler)`.
3. Record a cassette under `testdata/` and add a sub-test in `handler_test.go`.

